note E14 bound rule (negative): c[i & 127] is checked against 104 by omc, so the index is in 0..103 and may
note be 32..39: the store may hit the declared count field and must revoke it even with e14.
fn f c edit uchar 104 a view uchar 1 i ulong to ulong
put c and i 127 get a 0
if eq get c 32 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
